WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.310
Bring out your Number!

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:08.650
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.340
Xyz Summon!

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.320
Appear, Number 39!

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.840
Utopia!

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.870
Yuma used a Number?

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.000
He promised
that he wouldn’t use it!

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.750
Aero Shark attacks you directly!

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:29.210
Big Eater!

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:39.640
Yuma lost.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.310
Don’t bother me again!

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.350
This must be a joke.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.440
I used a Number,
but I still lost.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.450
I Special Summon UFO Turtle!

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:05.370
I’ll attack UFO Turtle
with Gagaga Magician!

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.080
I don’t understand Yuma.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:12.820
If I lost like that,
I couldn’t recover for a while.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.720
It gained ATK?

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.680
To summarize, Yuma
doesn’t have any pride.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.140
UFO Turtle attacks Gagaga Magician!

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.070
That’s twenty losses in a row.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.070
Damn!

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.470
I didn’t know you had
a spell card!

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.400
Let’s have another duel!

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.910
You want to keep going?

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.240
Of course!

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.700
My goal is to
become duel champion!

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.510
Keep bringing it on!

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:48.080
I can’t do this.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:52.750
Why?

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.170
In that case, you’re next,
class representative!

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.420
Wait!

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.640
Wait!

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.900
Tetsuo.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.290
I didn’t think Yuma was
that kind of person.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.350
That duel...

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.940
He said that he
wouldn’t use a Number.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.110
However...

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.370
That’s because Yuma is foolish—

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.140
I know he’s foolish!

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.950
Yuma is foolish
and gets carried away.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.980
But he was never a liar!

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.980
Tetsuo!

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:31.940
Yuma...

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.140
Shark.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.680
Join the fun.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.650
Bro!

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.030
Can you do something about Shark?

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.280
He’s arrogant!

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.640
You don’t understand, Ginji.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.290
Do you think we
really let him join us?

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:18.670
He’s a name
in the dueling world.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:23.260
If we make him a star in the underground dueling world,
we’ll make money without doing anything.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:26.170
We’ll make him
earn tons of money.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:31.010
My turn! I draw!

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.900
All right! Here I go!

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.740
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.870
They give color to each day;
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.790
Your kindness was harsh;
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:52.040
Freedom begins by accepting differences;
Dance and create the universe

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:59.420
In truth, I was sad
until I met you

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:05.990
I lied, thinking it was
easier to be alone

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:12.520
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.400
You’re the only one
who agreed with me

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.530
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.420
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.700
Everyone is not the same

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.620
That’s the reason for living

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:34.890
Even if the sounds
are dissonant at times

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:40.300
That’s why I never give up;
I believe my strength will get me through

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.220
I travel to
the edge of the world

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.010
The sights I see
with you are the truth

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.850
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:54.100
They give color to each day;
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.480
Your kindness was harsh;
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.150
Freedom begins by accepting differences;
Dance and create the universe

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:11.160
\hYuma and Shark: An Injury-Filled Tag Duel\h

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:11.160
Number 11:

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:13.950
Tetsuo!

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.560
Tetsuo, duel me again today!

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.770
I’m never going to
duel you again.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:22.710
Humph!

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:24.760
You’re so mean!

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.660
There are plenty of other opponents!

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.740
It’s pointless.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:33.770
In your current state,
you can’t defeat any duelist.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.190
Your strategies are always amateurish.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.650
But you currently don’t even
have those amateurish strategies.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.450
You simply attack repeatedly and pointlessly.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.360
What?

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.820
Shark is the source
of your irritation.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.290
It’s true that he’s
a fabulous duelist.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.790
He has talent.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.290
But that’s not
the only reason he won.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.240
What do you mean?

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:04.590
He researched your deck
and attacked the Numbers’ weak point.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.770
What do you know about him?

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:07.720
Well...

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:14.180
Something may have happened to Shark
after appearing in the national duel tournament.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:17.760
I heard that’s when
Shark began to stray.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.550
You’re really going to do it?

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.740
Of course.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.700
We’ll never get a second chance.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.350
Look.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.960
The centerpiece of the exhibition
is this super rare deck.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.690
No one knew where it was
for the longest time.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.410
“Chaos End Ruler - Ruler of the Beginning and the End”

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:42.840
But they randomly found it among
the museum’s recent donations, so it’s now on exhibit.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:46.340
I definitely want that deck!

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:50.510
But isn’t it dangerous
to rob a museum?

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.890
We can get arrested.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.720
So what?

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:59.190
You always said that you
want to do something big!

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.150
That’s true, but—

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:05.400
Don’t worry. We have this.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:09.070
A Number!

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.780
He’s right.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:17.370
Ever since we got them,
everything has been going our way.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.530
We won’t get captured!

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.990
The power of these cards
is protecting us.

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:25.710
But...

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:28.630
What? You don’t
want to do it?

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:30.050
Umm...

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:36.440
What are you doing here?

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:40.230
Since you heard our plans,
you’re going to participate.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.900
You’re coming with us, right?

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.360
Yeah, I don’t mind.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.670
All right, it’s decided.

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:54.070
We’re doing this tonight. Be ready.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.700
This is bad...

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:04.710
This time, we’re done for!

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.380
Leave the city while you can.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.490
You’re going to let me go?

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:14.840
But why?

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:16.550
Get out of here!

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:23.890
Huh?

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:27.200
That’s weird. It doesn’t open.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:28.610
Are you looking up something?

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:32.320
You rarely come to the library.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.490
Duel Monsters National Tournament?

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.160
I’m just checking something.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:47.540
Disgraced contender Ryoga Kamishiro...

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:51.050
It’s about Shark?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.010
Shark’s past...

00:08:53.460 --> 00:09:02.180
Contender Ryoga Kamishiro illegally looked at his opponent’s deck and was disqualified from the finals.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:12.070
Shark...

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.460
Shark peeked at his opponent’s deck?

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:17.530
It must be a lie!

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.530
But at the library...

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:23.250
I know because
I dueled against Shark.

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:26.580
A cheater wouldn’t duel like that!

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.560
My turn!

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:28.790
Now summon it!

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:31.550
Appear, Black Ray Lancer!

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:32.650
Yuma...

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:34.380
Hey!

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:39.130
You were hanging out with Shark!

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.440
Shark is going to steal cards?

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:50.460
Yeah. They’re breaking into the museum.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:51.690
It’s those cards’ fault!

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:56.150
They started acting differently
when they acquired those cards.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.610
They’re Numbers.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:02.120
They’re going to make
Shark take all the blame.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.030
He’ll be—

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:05.500
Wait, Yuma!

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:09.490
Let’s stay away from Shark.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:13.710
I have to go.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:14.760
Why?

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.660
Why are you doing
so much for Shark?

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:18.130
You’re wrong!

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:21.240
I’m not going for Shark.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.100
I’m going for myself!

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.600
I lied to myself.

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:31.610
I said that I wanted to free Shark,
but in reality, I wanted to win.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:35.070
I used a Number
because I wanted to win.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:38.320
I don’t want things
to end like this!

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.690
Where did Ginji go?

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.710
Forget about him.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.150
But that punk was—

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:54.890
It’s fine.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:57.720
Shark will work harder to compensate.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.630
Right?

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:29.330
Who are you?

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:34.500
I won’t let you
go any further.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.900
What?

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.430
You’re that hot-headed kid from before.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.280
Look, Yuma.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:45.390
If you want to go any further,
you have to defeat me in a duel first!

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.000
A duel?

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.640
What’s going on?

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:53.600
If you win,
I’ll give you my Number!

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:55.560
He’s risking his Number?

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:59.280
But if I win, you’ll leave
the museum alone!

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.240
That card is like ours.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.450
So this is called a Number.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:09.290
We’re very powerful
with just two cards.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.160
If we get that card,
we’ll be invincible.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.780
Bring it on, Rikuo and Kaio!

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:17.090
You’re gonna fight two-on-one?

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.960
Of course!

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:22.130
I won’t let you become
a card thief!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:25.550
I told you to never
bother me again.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.970
I won’t leave you alone!

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:31.020
They’re using you!

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:34.980
I know.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:38.730
But this is the only place
where I belong.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:39.730
You’re wrong!

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:42.150
You don’t belong there!

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.990
I’m not giving up.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:47.780
This time, I’ll make sure
you cut your ties with them!

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.380
You’re so pushy!

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.620
Why are you doing this?

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:53.120
Because we’re friends, of course!

00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:59.620
No! I’m not going!

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:01.090
Tetsuo!

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.010
It’s true that Yuma lied.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.970
But he’s now battling
with all his strength!

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.910
Is this how you want things
to be? You’re friends!

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.430
Enough talk.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:18.810
We’re reconsidering because
you’re willing to wager a Number.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:22.770
It’s not two-on-one. We’ll battle three-on-one.

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:24.320
Right, Ryoga?

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.320
Fine!

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:28.990
I don’t care
if it’s two or three!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.240
You can attack me all together!

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:40.380
Sorry, but
I’m teaming up with him.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:41.530
What?

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:44.090
You’re betraying us?

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:45.700
Shark?

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:48.060
Don’t get the wrong idea.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:51.060
I’m just tired
of them protecting me.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:55.070
Interesting. You’re
challenging us to a tag duel?

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:56.890
They’re idiots.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:02.990
Ryoga, you know what’s
going to happen to you.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.390
Here I go!

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:10.450
Duel Disk set!

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:15.000
D-Gazer set!

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:20.130
AR Vision Link complete.

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.810
Duel!

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.390
I’ll go first!

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.930
My turn! I draw!

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:34.960
I set a monster
in defense position!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:44.530
I set two cards
and end my turn.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:48.490
Yuma, I can tell that they’re
familiar with tag duels.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:49.390
Be careful.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:50.660
I know!

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:54.410
It’s my turn! I draw!

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:56.830
I summon Zubaba Knight!

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.500
I’ll do it!

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.790
I attack the set monster!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.750
Go, Zubaba Knight!

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.210
Wait, Yuma!

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:12.340
In a tag duel, you can’t attack
until all players take a turn.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.880
Really?

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:15.390
Then I end my turn!

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:17.130
What an amateur.

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:19.060
This duel will be
an easy victory.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:21.560
My turn! I draw!

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:25.850
I summon Pompadour Blizzardon!

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:30.240
I set two cards
and end my turn!

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.230
We’re invincible in a tag duel.

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:36.200
You’ll regret challenging us.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.410
My turn! I draw!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.130
I summon Big Jaws!

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.800
I Special Summon Shark Stickers!

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:58.460
When a Fish-Type monster is summoned,
I can Special Summon this monster from my hand.

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:00.760
There are two Level 3 monsters.

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:01.600
Will you do it?

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:06.060
I overlay Level 3 Big Jaws
and Shark Stickers!

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:09.400
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.090
Xyz Summon!

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:14.530
Appear, Submersible Carrier Aero Shark!

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:21.230
He Xyz Summoned
on his first turn!

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:23.210
Shark is incredible!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.420
I activate its effect!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:33.660
Once per turn, by using an Overlay Unit,
you take 400 points of damage for every card in my hand.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:34.800
I see.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:39.970
You can’t attack on the first turn,
but you can deal effect damage.

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:45.400
Since I have four cards in my hand,
I deal 1600 points of damage to Rikuo!

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:51.580
All right! It worked!

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.460
I knew you were
going to do that.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:01.830
I activate my trap!

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:04.950
Blizzard Egg Level 5!

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:15.200
When an effect deals damage, the player who took
the damage Special Summons a Level 5 monster from his hand.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:21.220
But if he can’t Special Summon,
he takes 500 points of damage.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.910
That means...

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:28.170
If Rikuo doesn’t have a Level 5 monster in his hand,
he will take an additional 500 points of damage.

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:29.230
It’s a dangerous risk.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:31.980
Level 5...

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:37.840
I Special Summon Level
5 Baggy Pants Lavasaurus!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.460
I’m next.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.150
I activate a trap!

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:49.900
Flame Egg Level 5!

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:59.600
When I take effect damage, my teammate Special Summons
a Level 5 monster from his hand.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:04.060
But if he can’t summon,
he takes 500 points of damage.

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:05.950
It’s the same thing again!

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:11.940
I Special Summon Level 5
Icebergdon in defense position!

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:20.240
He also had
a Level 5 monster.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.490
No way.

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:24.200
They instantly Special Summoned two monsters!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:28.110
Did you see our perfect combination?

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:32.170
No one can defeat
us in a tag duel.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:35.790
Why are they so confident?

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:38.180
There’s something wrong about this duel.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.840
Are they...

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.600
Here I go, Ryoga!

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.850
I activate my trap!

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.100
Glare Level 5!

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:53.520
For every Level 5 monster on our fields,
you take 500 points of damage.

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:57.360
There are two Level 5
monsters on our fields.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.430
That’s 1000 points of damage!

00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:01.490
Take this, traitor!

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:06.950
Shark!

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:12.080
You’re pathetic.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.480
I set two cards
and end my turn!

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:19.740
What’s up with this duel?

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:21.710
No one has attacked...

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:24.760
...but LP are going down.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.070
Calm down, Yuma.

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:30.460
If you don’t,
we won’t win this duel.

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:33.400
Oh yeah.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:38.940
In this duel, our futures
are on the line.

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:40.860
I can’t afford to lose.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:44.990
My turn! I draw!

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:48.790
I switch my monster from defense
position to attack position.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.870
Appear, Flamesaurus!

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:55.120
A tag duel?

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.170
Why are Yuma and Shark together?

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:00.670
Flamesaurus’s flip effect activates!

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:04.640
This card gains one Level,
making it Level 5!

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:10.140
I overlay Level 5 Flamesaurus
and Baggy Pants Lavasaurus!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.790
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network.

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:16.110
Xyz Summon!

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:18.690
Appear, Number 61!

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:25.060
Volcasaurus!

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:47.680
That’s their Number!

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.140
A Number!

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:53.100
You did it, bro!

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:54.890
Victory is ours.

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:57.770
I’ll show you
how terrifying we are.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.760
I activate Volcasaurus’s effect!

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:05.280
By using one Overlay Unit,
one of your monsters is destroyed...

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:09.740
...and you take damage
equal to its ATK!

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:12.540
I destroy Aero Shark!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:15.040
Mag Max!

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:26.260
Ryoga, you take damage equal to Aero Shark’s ATK
for 1900 points of damage!

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:30.180
Shark!

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:34.430
This isn’t the time
to worry about others.

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:36.570
You’re next.

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:38.360
I destroy Zubaba Knight.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:40.230
Mag Max!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:48.370
Yuma!

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.330
What power!

00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:58.660
Now you know
how powerful we are!

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:01.440
Your Number is ours!

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:14.960
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:16.940
This week’s quiz:

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:19.670
There are three
types of trap cards.

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:22.850
Normal Traps, Counter Traps and...

00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:24.820
What’s the last type?

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:35.050
Today’s test is hard;
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:35.050 --> 00:22:39.880
I want to go home and watch TV;
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:54.650
Anyway, tests are hard;
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.650 --> 00:22:59.480
Average scores in science and social studies;
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:02.480
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.770
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:07.190
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:08.820
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:13.810
Let’s say I wrote
the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.810 --> 00:23:18.080
Will that change the future a year
or a decade from now?

00:23:18.650 --> 00:23:23.750
The world I drew
at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:28.720
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:33.300
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:37.310
Nothing is correct!

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:43.310
There’s something strange about this duel.

00:23:43.920 --> 00:23:49.440
Even if they’re cheating,
we’ll fight fair-and-square and win!

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:51.950
I was afraid to lose.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:53.970
Stop laughing!

00:23:53.970 --> 00:23:55.410
Yuma, let’s win.

00:23:56.010 --> 00:23:58.370
Shark gave me this card...

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:00.750
You can figure it out.

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:09.970
\hUtopic Combo! Armored Xyz Activates!\h

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:06.240
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Utopic Combo! Armored Xyz Activates!”

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:09.970
\hUtopic Combo! Armored Xyz Activates!\h

00:24:06.240 --> 00:24:09.140
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.890 --> 00:24:13.870
The answer is...

00:24:13.870 --> 00:24:17.150
A Continuous Trap!

00:24:17.150 --> 00:24:23.890
Use these three traps
to silence your opponent!
